WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.634
♪ (SOFT MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:03.736
CECILIA ALDARONDO:
 Imagine you had a nightmare

00:00:04.336 --> 00:00:07.673
 where you had to relive
 your adolescence.

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:12.211
 My memories shine
 almost like a diamond.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.647
 But not because I loved them.

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:16.049
♪ (MUSIC DEFLATES) ♪

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:17.550
 Because I hate them.

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:20.419
♪ (UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:20.919 --> 00:00:21.987
 When I was a teenager,

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.290
 I would imagine myself
 falling in love...

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.493
 I love him, I love him,
 I love him, I love him...

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.194
 ...for all my crushes.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:31.331
 I was trying to be whatever
 they wanted me to be.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:34.099
 I was always just acting.

00:00:34.199 --> 00:00:35.067
DIRECTOR: Roll, please.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.502
Oh. Hi, Joel.

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:37.803
JOEL: (OVER PHONE)
 Uh, who's this?

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:38.771
ALDARONDO: Oh, um...

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:39.939
-DIRECTOR: Cut!
-(LAUGHS)

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:41.207
♪ (MUSIC DARKENS) ♪

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:45.010
ALDARONDO:
 I think of these recreations
 as like an emotional exorcism.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:46.045
Are you lost?

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:47.513
I sit there.

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:48.781
Get out of her seat.

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:52.485
I am truly haunted
by these things.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.421
 And one of the things
 that I can't get past

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:57.022
 is why they still bother me.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.791
♪ (UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.727
The guy organizing
the reunion posted this.

00:01:01.827 --> 00:01:03.096
"Dress: Winter Park."

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:05.498
This is like blood red,
"I'm gonna kill them all."

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:08.133
-Resentment red.
-(LAUGHING) Resentment red.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.770
ALDARONDO: Oh, God.
A country club.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.773
I just feel like
this is a huge mistake.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:14.907
(GROANS)

00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:16.342
(LAUGHING)
Don't make me go in there.

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:17.576
♪ (MUSIC BRIGHTENS) ♪

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.779
SPEAKER: I can understand
 being traumatized.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:22.615
 But why you continue,
 all these years later,

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:25.985
 to allow them to have
 all this power over you

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.252
blows my mind.

00:01:27.786 --> 00:01:29.621
ALDARONDO: Why would I
 remember this for 25 years

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.158
if I didn't know then
that it was that bad?

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.125
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:37.797
 The paradox of going back is
to have to succumb, once again,

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:41.468
 to that sense of yourself
 as totally inconsequential.

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:44.838
 So, why on earth
 would I go back?

